    "result_text": "All 279 tests pass. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field on owner creation: `\"local\"` when the new owner's city is the single most common city among existing owners at that moment, otherwise `\"remote\"`.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established pattern for creation-time computed fields (like `namesakeCount`, `sharesHousehold`, `membershipTier`), the value is computed before save and persisted, so it survives the GET round-trip the acceptance tests use.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`DetermineLocality.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners per city (case-insensitive), finds the strict single maximum, and sets `locality` to `\"local\"` if the new owner's city is that unique most-common city, else `\"remote\"`. A tie for the top count means no single most common city \u2192 `\"remote\"`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `determineLocality` into the pipeline between `determineSharesHousehold` and `save` (under the transaction governance).\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `locality` column with getter/setter.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `locality VARCHAR(10)` column.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property (enum `local`/`remote`) to the Owner schema, generating `OwnerDto.LocalityEnum`.\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an explicit mapping for `locality`. This was necessary because the generated `LocalityEnum`'s constant names (`LOCAL`) differ from its JSON values (`local`), so MapStruct's default `Enum.valueOf` fails; the mapping uses `LocalityEnum.fromValue(...)` instead. (This differs from `membershipTier`, where the constant name and value happen to coincide.)\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp18Tests` acceptance test now passes, along with the full suite (279 tests).",
